<aside class="gm-limitations not-prose" aria-labelledby="gm-limitations-title">
  <p class="gm-limitations-eyebrow">Interpretation boundary</p>
  <h3 id="gm-limitations-title">Limitations</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>The exercises used simulated rather than real capital.</li>
    <li>
      Short-duration sessions across different cohorts, market paths and news
      sequences do not constitute a repeatable performance record or controlled
      experiment.
    </li>
    <li>
      The principal buy-side and sell-side results came from different dates;
      the page is a role-specific process study rather than a claim of one
      uniformly strong dual-role event.
    </li>
    <li>
      Several portal metrics, acronym definitions and the composite weighting
      formula are proprietary or incompletely documented.
    </li>
    <li>
      The portal retains the original 29 July asset-management ordering. Event
      administration subsequently voided the displayed first-place result, so
      the public page reports both the displayed 2nd-of-102 rank and the
      highest-valid post-event status rather than converting it to an
      unqualified first place.
    </li>
    <li>
      The platform labels the $3.80 million result differently across the
      detailed and leaderboard views, while the reported portfolio-value field
      does not mechanically reconcile with P&amp;L and commission. The values
      are reproduced as separate portal-reported metrics rather than
      independently reconciled.
    </li>
    <li>
      The 29 July portfolio finished 99.5% invested in equities. The strong
      return, Sharpe ratio and BSRM platform subscore therefore should not be
      interpreted as evidence of a conservatively positioned final portfolio.
    </li>
    <li>
      Rankings across cohorts are not perfectly comparable, and the 22 July
      asset-management P&amp;L denominator remains unresolved between 153 total
      participants and 148 manually counted ranked entries.
    </li>
    <li>
      The portal uses different P&amp;L field labels across sessions, preventing
      a mechanical comparison of every financial field in the session ledger.
    </li>
    <li>
      No full transaction-level export is available for an independent
      reconstruction of the portfolios, dealer books or exact intraday
      allocation paths.
    </li>
    <li>
      The 29 July sell-side phase recorded strong execution and control metrics
      but negative total P&amp;L, illustrating that operational discipline does
      not guarantee a favourable inventory outcome.
    </li>
  </ul>
</aside>

